      "message": "You had added `{: #TOC-How-strings-get-translated }` here to customize the page fragment (presumably to make it compatible with the way the Sites page worked).\n\nUnfortunately, it looks like there\u0027s a bug and the TOC-generating plugin that I\u0027m using isn\u0027t actually picking up the customized identifiers.\n\nI\u0027ve changed this back to the default (which does work), and fixed the links on this page that cross-link to the different sections.\n\nHowever, if we have documentation elsewhere that is relying on http://chromium.org/developers-design-documents/ui-localization#TOC-How-strings-get-translated to still work, this won\u0027t work right.\n\nIf so, I think we have two choices:\n\n1) Don\u0027t worry about it (the URL will still link to the page and people may be able to figure it out)\n\n2) I can fix the TOC-generating plugin to be Sites-compatible (and to handle the custom IDs; I\u0027ll do the latter regardless, but I don\u0027t actually like Sites having used TOC- in the IDs, so I kinda prefer the new format).\n\n3) We can insert `\u003ca name\u003d\"TOC-How-strings-get-translated\"\u003e` into the heading.\n\nLet me know which of the above you might like?",
